title: Nuremberg
subtitle: The Independents go home to the SPD.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 9
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.leader();
RG.news('Nuremberg: the Independents rejoin the SPD', 2);
Q.e22_had_uspd = Q.uspd_exists ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.uspd_exists) {
    Q.spd_seats = Math.min(Q.spd_seats + Q.uspd_seats, Q.uspd_split ? 171 : 999);
    Q.uspd_seats = 0;
    Q.uspd_exists = 0;
    Q.uspd_in_government = 0;
}
// Reuter, kept in January, goes where his ideas lead him
Q.e22_reuter_leaves = (Q.e22_friesland == 2 && Q.lead_code != 1) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e22_reuter_leaves) {
    RG.district('berlin', {members: -0.06});
    RG.news('Ernst Reuter leaves the party for the SPD', 2);
}
Q.e22_unity_possible = ((Q.lead_code == 1 && Q.spd_relation >= 30) || Q.levi_in_party == 1) ? 1 : 0;
!}

= Nuremberg

[? if e22_had_uspd = 1 : On 24 September, in Nuremberg, what is left of the Independent Social Democrats votes to rejoin the SPD, six years after the split over the war credits. Georg Ledebour and a handful of others keep the old name alive. ?][? if e22_had_uspd = 0 : In Nuremberg the SPD holds a congress of unity with the last social democrats who stood apart from it. ?] The SPD is the largest party in the Reichstag again. Its new left wing, Crispien and Dittmann, dislikes the coalition with the Centre.

[? if e22_reuter_leaves = 1 : Ernst Reuter, whom the party kept in January, goes over to the SPD in the same week and takes a good part of the Berlin organisation with him. ?][? if e22_unity_possible = 1 : Some on both sides ask why there should be two workers' parties at all. A few of them sit in our Zentrale. ?]

- @court: Appeal to the Independents' rank and file to join us instead.
- @offer: Offer the SPD a common fight for wages and the eight-hour day.
- @denounce: Denounce the reunion.
- @unity: Propose one party of the German workers.

@court
subtitle: Whole branches cross over in Saxony and Thuringia.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_reunification = 1;
RG.district('saxony', {members: 0.05});
RG.district('thuringia', {members: 0.07});
Q.spd_relation -= 4;
!}

Ledebour will not come. In Leipzig, Gera and Suhl whole branches of the old USPD join us rather than go back to the party of Noske.

@offer
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The executive will file it. Many branches will not.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any offer to the SPD.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.e22_reunification = 2;
Q.spd_relation += 7;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Our open letter proposes a common fight for wages, the eight-hour day and against the monarchist leagues. The executive files it.

@denounce
subtitle: The SPD's new left wing is offended.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_reunification = 3;
Q.spd_relation -= 8;
Q.militancy += 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

*Die Rote Fahne* greets the reunion with a cartoon of Noske welcoming Crispien home with a rope.

@unity
subtitle: The end of the party as a party of its own. Moscow will expel us all.
view-if: e22_unity_possible = 1
choose-if: spd_relation >= 40 and lock_united_front = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The social democrats will not have us, or the party would never accept it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_reunification = 4;
Q.ending_id = 5;
RG.ledger('The party voted to join one party of the German workers with the SPD.', 'e22_unity');
!}

After weeks of talks, a congress of unity meets in Berlin. The party of Luxemburg and Liebknecht votes, by a narrow majority, to become the left wing of one German workers' party.

- @end: See how it ends.

@end
go-to: game_over
